        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Delhi</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1052 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">Anang Pal of the Tomara dynasty built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lal-kot">Lal Kot</a> in 1052 CE; the Tomaras are placed earlier too, and tradition links the site with Indraprastha, the city of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamuna">Yamuna</a> river, chiefly on its right bank, between the Yamuna floodplains and the Delhi Ridge, in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</span></div>
